  "description": "OFABII crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C88 H176 Dy8 O47 P6 2-,2(C3 H10 N1 1+). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy6 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy7 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy8 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 9 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.642-3.919 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 94.07-110.41°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula (NH3iPr)2[Dy8(O3PtBu)6(μ3-OH)2(O2CtBu)12(H2O)(HOiBu)]. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula). Article name explicitly identifies I(II).",
